[1m[38;5;231mHow does the notification actually reach a teammate?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mIn-app only (bell icon)[39m
  [38;5;246mA badge and a list inside the app. No outbound infrastructure at all — it's a query over the change log plus a [39m
  [38;5;246mread/unread marker. By far the smallest system, and it works offline of any mail provider.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Email
  [38;5;246mReaches people who aren't in the app. Adds an outbound queue, retries, templates, bounce handling, unsubscribe links,
[39m  [38;5;246mand digest batching so you don't send 40 mails an hour. Roughly doubles the subsystem.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] Browser push
  [38;5;246mReal-time even when the tab is closed. Adds service workers, VAPID keys, per-device subscription records, and [39m
  [38;5;246mpermission prompts — plus the browser can revoke it silently.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Chat integration (Slack/Teams)
  [38;5;246mLands where the team already is. Depends on an external API, its auth model, and its rate limits; usually done after [39m
  [38;5;246min-app works.[39m
